{"approved_definition": "Restraint of actions, inclinations, and impulses likely to upset or harm others and violate social expectations or norms. Derives from the requirement that individuals inhibit inclinations that might disrupt and undermine smooth interaction and group functioning (cf. Freud, 1930; Kohn & Schooler, 1983; Parsons, 1951).", "core_value": "conformity", "sources": [{"entry_id": "7c712a0a:entry:6", "journal_entry": "Back from the conference for a week now and people at work keep asking how it was. I say it was great, very inspiring, lots of good ideas. Which is true. But when they ask what I am going to do differently, I do not have a good answer. Learn Go? Propose a rewrite? Those feel like someone else's moves.

